# 必考词 Unit16
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2023红宝书考研英语词汇-必考词
# 描述: 必考词Unit16核心高频词汇

{{outcome}}{/ˈaʊtkʌm/}}{n. 结果；后果}}{{The outcome of the election surprised everyone.}}

{{outline}}{/ˈaʊtlaɪn/}}{n. 轮廓；大纲；v. 概述}}{{The professor outlined the main points of the lecture.}}

{{outlook}}{/ˈaʊtlʊk/}}{n. 展望；前景}}{{The economic outlook for next year is uncertain.}}

{{output}}{/ˈaʊtpʊt/}}{n. 产量；输出}}{{The factory's output has doubled since last year.}}

{{outstanding}}{/aʊtˈstændɪŋ/}}{adj. 杰出的；未解决的}}{{She received an award for her outstanding contributions to science.}}

{{overall}}{/ˌəʊvərˈɔːl/}}{adj. 全面的；adv. 总体上}}{{The overall quality of the product has improved significantly.}}

{{overcome}}{/ˌəʊvərˈkʌm/}}{v. 克服；战胜}}{{She overcame many obstacles to achieve her goals.}}

{{overlook}}{/ˌəʊvərˈlʊk/}}{v. 忽视；俯瞰}}{{Do not overlook the importance of细节 in the experiment.}}

{{overseas}}{/ˌəʊvərˈsiːz/}}{adv./adj. 海外（的）}}{{Many students choose to study overseas for better opportunities.}}

{{overtake}}{/ˌəʊvərˈteɪk/}}{v. 赶上；超过}}{{China has overtaken Japan as the world's second-largest economy.}}

{{owe}}{/əʊ/}}{v. 欠；归功于}}{{I owe my success to the support of my family.}}

{{pace}}{/peɪs/}}{n. 步伐；速度}}{{The pace of technological change is accelerating.}}

{{panel}}{/ˈpænl/}}{n. 专家小组；面板}}{{A panel of experts reviewed the research proposal.}}

{{paradox}}{/ˈpærədɒks/}}{n. 悖论；矛盾的事物}}{{It is a paradox that the richest country has the most poor people.}}

{{parallel}}{/ˈpærəlel/}}{adj. 平行的；类似的}}{{The two roads run parallel to each other for miles.}}

{{participate}}{/pɑːˈtɪsɪpeɪt/}}{v. 参与；参加}}{{All students are encouraged to participate in extracurricular activities.}}

{{particular}}{/pəˈtɪkjələr/}}{adj. 特定的；挑剔的}}{{Is there a particular reason for your absence yesterday?}}

{{passion}}{/ˈpæʃn/}}{n. 热情；激情}}{{He has a passion for music that started in childhood.}}

{{passive}}{/ˈpæsɪv/}}{adj. 被动的；消极的}}{{A passive approach to learning is less effective.}}

{{pattern}}{/ˈpætərn/}}{n. 模式；图案}}{{Scientists have identified a pattern in the data.}}

{{perceive}}{/pəˈsiːv/}}{v. 感知；理解}}{{People perceive the world differently based on their experiences.}}

{{percentage}}{/pəˈsentɪdʒ/}}{n. 百分比；比例}}{{What percentage of the population lives in urban areas?}}

{{perception}}{/pəˈsepʃn/}}{n. 认知；看法}}{{Public perception of the company has improved recently.}}

{{perform}}{/pəˈfɔːrm/}}{v. 执行；表演}}{{The students performed well in the national examination.}}

{{permanent}}{/ˈpɜːrmənənt/}}{adj. 永久的；持久的}}{{The injury left a permanent scar on his arm.}}

{{permit}}{/pəˈmɪt/}}{v. 允许；n. 许可证}}{{Smoking is not permitted inside the building.}}

{{persist}}{/pəˈsɪst/}}{v. 坚持；持续}}{{He persisted in his efforts despite repeated failures.}}

{{perspective}}{/pəˈspektɪv/}}{n. 观点；视角}}{{Traveling helps you gain a broader perspective on life.}}

{{pessimistic}}{/ˌpesɪˈmɪstɪk/}}{adj. 悲观的}}{{She is pessimistic about the chances of success.}}

{{phenomenon}}{/fəˈnɒmɪnən/}}{n. 现象}}{{Globalization is a complex phenomenon with many aspects.}}

{{philosophy}}{/fɪˈlɒsəfi/}}{n. 哲学；人生观}}{{His philosophy of life is to help others whenever possible.}}

{{physical}}{/ˈfɪzɪkl/}}{adj. 物质的；身体的}}{{Physical exercise is important for maintaining good health.}}

{{pioneer}}{/ˌpaɪəˈnɪər/}}{n. 先驱；v. 开拓}}{{She was a pioneer in the field of genetic research.}}

{{policy}}{/ˈpɒləsi/}}{n. 政策；方针}}{{The government announced a new policy on education reform.}}

{{politics}}{/ˈpɒlətɪks/}}{n. 政治；政治学}}{{She has been interested in politics since college.}}

{{portion}}{/ˈpɔːrʃn/}}{n. 部分；一份}}{{A large portion of the budget is spent on education.}}

{{positive}}{/ˈpɒzətɪv/}}{adj. 积极的；肯定的}}{{A positive attitude can help you overcome difficulties.}}

{{possess}}{/pəˈzes/}}{v. 拥有；具有}}{{She possesses excellent communication skills.}}

{{potential}}{/pəˈtenʃl/}}{adj. 潜在的；n. 潜力}}{{Every child has the potential to succeed with proper guidance.}}

{{poverty}}{/ˈpɒvərti/}}{n. 贫困；贫乏}}{{Millions of people around the world still live in poverty.}}
